Using the templates:
1. Choose the button-pressing or contextual template
2. No guide file yet: 
    - Right click on the relevant template file name and click 'Copy'
    - Right click on product folder name (Ultra, Panopto etc.) and click 'Paste'
    - Open the folder and find the copied file.
    - Right click on the file name and click 'Rename'. Enter guide file name (eg. using-a-template)
3. Guide file already exists:
    - Open the relevant template file and copy all the text.
    - Open your new guide file and paste in the text.  
6. Right click on the file name to open the file.
7. Add content. ALL TEXT CAPS is to replace, eg: LINK URL. <!-- commented out text --> is instructions for you - either delete or leave commented. Use the Style Guide.
8. Save file.
9. In GitHub desktop, commit and push to origin.
10. Celebrate with a biscuit (round, of course!)

Key syntax:
- headings: # H1, ## H2, ## H3 etc.
- bold text: **bold text**
- link: [LINK TEXT](LINK URL)
- image: ![ALT TEXT](images/IMAGE FILE NAME "OPTIONAL IMAGE TITLE")
- ordered list (numbered): 1. item one / 2. item two etc. (don't have to be in numerical order)
- unordered list (bullet): - item one / - item two etc. Don't use for process steps.
- admonition: !!! ADMONITION TITLE (eg, !!! Summary)

